@{
    ViewData["Title"] = L["Privacy Policy"].Value;
}
<article class="s-panel s-rise s-legal">
    <h1 class="s-h1 s-gold-text">@L["Privacy Policy"]</h1>
    <p>@L["This is what Souls Online stores about you, why, and how to have it removed."]</p>
    <h2>@L["What we store"]</h2>
    <p>@L["Your player name, a hash of your password (never the password itself), the hero, cards, coins, quests and ratings of your account, your games and their replays, and the messages you write in game chat."]</p>
    <h2>@L["Discord"]</h2>
    <p>@L["If you play through Discord, we store your Discord user id to know your account, and use your Discord name to suggest your player name. For Linked Roles we keep the access tokens Discord gives us, encrypted, only to show your Souls rank on Discord. We see nothing else of your Discord account."]</p>
    <h2>@L["Cookies"]</h2>
    <p>@L["Souls uses cookies only to keep you logged in, to protect forms and to remember your language. There are no tracking or advertising cookies."]</p>
    <h2>@L["Sharing"]</h2>
    <p>@L["Your data is not sold or shared. Your player name, rank and games are visible to other players. The service runs on a server of our own."]</p>
    <h2>@L["Removal"]</h2>
    <p>@L["To have your account and its data removed, or to ask what we store about you, open an issue in the Souls repository on GitHub. Unlinking Souls in Discord's settings stops Linked Roles at once."]</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/pa-research/Souls/issues">github.com/pa-research/Souls</a></p>
</article>
